BRIEF: session 19, the minority-modality loss on directories of GitHub repositories, pre-registered before any repository is listed

Primary family of three tests under E1 (c minus a in the minority cells that keep a same-modality sibling; c minus d where c is a strict subset), owner-weighted with 10,000 owner resamples and Bonferroni intervals, a smallest effect of +0.05 and a minimum of 100 owners. scripts/fetch_gh.py (pool by random days, harvest by tarball, rebuild by commit, commit history), scripts/s19.py (corpus counts, the registered tests, commit-subject queries), scripts/s19_run.sh (the pod driver), scripts/s19_selftest.py (the whole pipeline on synthetic repositories behind a local stand-in for the API: passes). eval.py gains the row cs (square-root budget); a, c and d are unchanged rank for rank with or without it (checked by the self-test). manifest.py gains --dir-prefix. reports/panel_2026-10-04.md: the three blind reviews of the SIGIR version and the second round on the plan.

